@page "/Home"
<MudText Class="mx-4 px-4 ym-4 pm-4" Typo="Typo.h2">Home</MudText>  
<MudDivider Class="mb-4 pb-4"/>
<MudText Class="mx-4 px-4 ym-4 pm-4" Typo="Typo.h5">Introduction</MudText>
<MudText Class="mx-6 px-6 ym-4 pm-4" Typo="Typo.body1">
    The Trajectory service owns survey runs, calculated or imported trajectories, interpolation and uncertainty
    calculations, anti-collision results, and the shared identity and feature catalogs used to classify them.
    Engineering values are stored in canonical SI units; depths and vertical coordinates are metres relative to WGS84.
</MudText>

<MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" Class="mx-6 my-4">
    Persisted calculation cases and results are durable. They are never removed automatically because they are older
    than 90 days; deletion occurs only through an explicit user or API operation.
</MudAlert>

<MudDivider Class="my-4 py-4"/>
<MudText Class="mx-4 px-4 ym-4 pm-4" Typo="Typo.h5">Data Input</MudText>
<MudText Class="mx-6 px-6 ym-4 pm-4" Typo="Typo.body1">
    Use Survey Runs to upload measured MD, inclination, and azimuth data, then create trajectories from those runs.
    Large station and calculation-result arrays use chunked transfer. Backup / Restore exports dependency-closed,
    versioned JSON documents and restores them atomically. Catalog UUIDs match exactly by default; normalized-name
    mapping is available only as an explicit restore opt-in.
</MudText>

<MudDivider Class="my-4 py-4"/>
<MudText Class="mx-4 px-4 ym-4 pm-4" Typo="Typo.h5">Service access</MudText>
<MudText Class="mx-6 px-6 ym-4 pm-4" Typo="Typo.body1">
    The REST/OpenAPI contract is available under <a href="/Trajectory/api/swagger">/Trajectory/api/swagger</a> and
    MCP under <code>/Trajectory/api/mcp</code>. MCP callers should use the bounded trajectory and survey-run search
    tools for discovery, then fetch selected records by UUID. Durable updates and deletes require the opaque
    <code>LastModificationDate</code> value from the latest read.
</MudText>

 <MudStack Spacing="2" Class="my-4 py-4">
    <MudButton Class="shades-text text-white"
        Variant="Variant.Filled"
        Style="@($"background:{HideColors(showAddTutorial)};")"
        OnClick="ShowHideAddTutorial">@(showAddTutorial ? "Hide add table tutorial" : "Show add table tutorial")        
    </MudButton>
    @* Add a video using the webm format*@
    <MudCollapse Expanded="showAddTutorial">                
        <center>
            <video width="960" height="540" autoplay loop muted>
                <source src="videos/dummyvideo.webm" type="video/webm">
                Your browser does not support the video tag.
            </video>
        </center>
    </MudCollapse>
</MudStack>


@code{
    private bool showAddTutorial = true;
    private bool showUploadTutorial = true;
    private bool showViewTutorial = true;

    private void ShowHideAddTutorial()
    {
        showAddTutorial = !showAddTutorial;
    } 
    private string HideColors(bool expandBool)
    {
        if (expandBool)
        {
            return MudBlazor.Colors.Indigo.Lighten1;
        }
        else
        {
            return MudBlazor.Colors.Indigo.Darken4;            
        }
    }
}
